ticles. A trivial all-not-relevant rule would agree with the pilot coder on 31/34 = 91.2%. The paper already says the comparison is indicative only, so this is not reported as a numerical defect.","Table 5: the sum of the two road-system reference segments (m0–1492 and m0–641) is 2,133 m against a reported length of 2,132 m. This is rounding-compatible and not reported.","Table 7: the text says 'between a third and a half' of projects, but the counts range from 4 of 44 (about 9 percent) to 24 of 44 (about 55 percent). The 'most of the other groups' qualifier keeps this approximate-language point below the materiality threshold.","Structured table CSV/markdown cells were not used for cell assignment, following the parser-quality warnings. Values were read from the page text, with the table PNGs consulted only where the parser audit had compared them. Table 3 and 4 body cells match the page text. Figure 1's chart was read from page_images/page_004.png, and Figures 2 and 3 from their crops."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"complete","scope_description":"Numerical audit of the whole 18-page paper: central pilot, validation, full-run and listing-data claims in full_text.md, all nine tables and four figures, and the appendix definitions, with recomputation of counts, percentages, sums and shares where the denominators were stated.","checks_completed":["Read the parser-quality output and used page text and page images instead of the structured table cells","Recomputed the pilot funnel (70 hits, 36 duplicates, 34 unique, 49%, 15%), the coding split 5+8+21, and 2/34, 5/34 and 1/34 shares","Recomputed Tables 3 and 4 (marginals, 33/34 = 97%) and compared them with the text and the abstract","Checked Table 2 article counts against Section 3.1.4 and Figure 1","Checked Table 6 sums (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 14-of-15 county count, and the 92 and 43 headline counts against the abstract, introduction and conclusion","Checked 96 articles and 44 projects (footnote 3), 18+2